/users/golergka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/comments/601959284","html_url":"https://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/issues/5729#issuecomment-601959284","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/5729","id":601959284,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYwMTk1OTI4NA==","user":{"login":"golergka","id":929735,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyOTczNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/929735?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka","html_url":"https://github.com/golergka","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-03-21T00:01:33Z","updated_at":"2020-03-21T00:03:21Z","body":"So, it seems that it's failing here:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/blob/4ed79c9cf9ad0f1e51930159dfdab8c1e8549339/src/driver/postgres/PostgresQueryRunner.ts#L317-L328\r\n\r\nWhile trying to create an up migration for a new enum. But it's not a new enum! It should use the same enum that was created before.\r\n\r\nI digged the code that checks if enum exists already, and found this:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/blob/4ed79c9cf9ad0f1e51930159dfdab8c1e8549339/src/driver/postgres/PostgresQueryRunner.ts#L1826-L1837\r\n\r\nApparently, table name is included in the generated enum name - so, although it's the same enum type on both columns, TypeORM tries to create a new type for each table that uses this enum.\r\n\r\nIf I understood all that correctly (and it's very possible that I didn't), that seems like a very strange design choice and defeats the whole purpose of user-defined data types.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/comments/601959284/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"golergka","id":929735,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyOTczNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/929735?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka","html_url":"https://github.com/golergka","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/comments/601962444","html_url":"https://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/issues/5729#issuecomment-601962444","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/5729","id":601962444,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYwMTk2MjQ0NA==","user":{"login":"golergka","id":929735,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyOTczNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/929735?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka","html_url":"https://github.com/golergka","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-03-21T00:15:36Z","updated_at":"2020-03-21T00:15:36Z","body":"Found a workaround!\r\n\r\nIn the code that decides how an enum should be named, there is mention that I could specify the enum name explicitly:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/blob/4ed79c9cf9ad0f1e51930159dfdab8c1e8549339/src/driver/postgres/PostgresQueryRunner.ts#L1992-L2000\r\n\r\nSo, I put it into my user entity (just in case, although the name stayed the same):\r\n\r\n```ts\r\n@Entity()\r\n// We have to create a composite index for it to be a target of a foregn key\r\n@Index(\"user_login_method\", [\"id\", \"loginMethod\"], { unique: true })\r\nexport class User {\r\n\r\n    @PrimaryGeneratedColumn()\r\n    id: number;\r\n\r\n    @Column({\r\n        type: \"enum\",\r\n        enum: UserLoginMethod,\r\n        enumName: \"user_loginmethod_enum\"\r\n    })\r\n    loginMethod: UserLoginMethod;\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd then into my new table, too:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\n@Entity()\r\nexport class UserDeviceId {\r\n\r\n    @Column({\r\n        type: \"enum\",\r\n        enum: UserLoginMethod,\r\n        enumName: \"user_loginmethod_enum\"\r\n    })\r\n    userLoginMethod: UserLoginMethod;\r\n\r\n    @OneToOne(type => User, { primary: true })\r\n    @JoinColumn([\r\n        { name: \"userId\", referencedColumnName: \"id\" },\r\n        { name: \"userLoginMethod\", referencedColumnName: \"loginMethod\" }\r\n    ])\r\n    user: User;\r\n\r\n    @Column({ unique: true })\r\n    @Index()\r\n    deviceId: string;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd now it uses the same type name for both.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/comments/601962444/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"golergka","id":929735,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyOTczNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/929735?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka","html_url":"https://github.com/golergka","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/golergka